 133+ 6453              // (+loop)      n --
 134+ 6453              // compiled by +LOOP. it uses the top two values of return-stack to
 135+ 6453              // keep track of index and limit, they are accessed via I and I'
 136+ 6453              // Add n to the loop index. If the loop index did not cross the boundary
 137+ 6453              // between the loop limit minus one and the loop limit, continue execution
 138+ 6453              // at the beginning of the loop. Otherwise, discard the current loop control
 139+ 6453              // parameters and continue execution immediately following the loop.
